# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a change
#
# Syntax: <path pattern> <@user or @org/team> ...
# The LAST matching pattern wins. Agents are not GitHub users, so ownership here is expressed with
# human/team handles; module ownership for agents is enforced by `python scripts/tp.py pr-check`.
#
# Replace `@your-handle` with real accounts, then delete these instructions.

# Default: everything needs the project owner's review.
*                                   @your-handle

# --- Process integrity: only the human changes the rules -------------------------------
/state/**                           @your-handle
/modules/**                         @your-handle
/docs/project/**                    @your-handle
/docs/agents/**                     @your-handle
/agents/**                          @your-handle
/docs/workflows/**                  @your-handle
/AGENTS.md                          @your-handle
/HOW_TO_USE.ipynb                   @your-handle
/.github/**                         @your-handle

# --- Framework plumbing: reviewed by whoever owns the toolchain --------------------------
/scripts/**                         @your-handle

# --- Module source code: assign real reviewers per module as decomposition lands ---------
# /src/auth/**                      @backend-reviewer
# /src/dashboard/**                 @frontend-reviewer

# --- Generated evidence: review is optional, but keep an eye on reports -------------------
/reports/**                         @your-handle
/handoffs/**                        @your-handle
